To consume a GraphQL endpoint in your React.js project, you can use Apollo Client, which is a powerful GraphQL client for managing state and fetching GraphQL data. Here's how you can add Apollo Client to your project:

First, install the necessary dependencies:
```bash
npm install @apollo/client graphql
```

Then, you can create an ApolloClient instance and set up the provider in your React application. You'll typically do this in your index.js or App.js file.

```javascript
// index.js or App.js

import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
import App from './App';
import { ApolloClient, InMemoryCache, ApolloProvider } from '@apollo/client';

const client = new ApolloClient({
  uri: 'YOUR_GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT_URL',
  cache: new InMemoryCache()
});

ReactDOM.render(
  <ApolloProvider client={client}>
    <App />
  </ApolloProvider>,
  document.getElementById('root')
);
```

Replace 'YOUR_GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT_URL' with the actual URL of your GraphQL endpoint.

