To create a new map of objects containing the category `uniqueId` and the question `uniqueId`, you can iterate over each category in `catData`, then iterate over each question in the `questions` field of each category. For each question, you can create a new object containing the category `uniqueId` and the question `uniqueId`, and collect these objects into a new array.

Here's the completed function:

```javascript
const createQIdMap = (catData = []) => {
  if (!catData || !catData.length) {
    return [];
  }

  // Initialize an empty array to store the resulting map
  const qIdMap = [];

  // Iterate over each category
  catData.forEach(category => {
    // Check if the category has questions
    if (category.questions && category.questions.length > 0) {
      // Iterate over each question in the category
      category.questions.forEach(question => {
        // Create a new object containing category uniqueId and question uniqueId
        const qIdObj = {
          categoryUniqueId: category.uniqueId,
          questionUniqueId: question.uniqueId
        };

        // Add the new object to the resulting map array
        qIdMap.push(qIdObj);
      });
    }
  });

  return qIdMap;
};

// Example usage
